<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 1 August, from 30 BCE to 1944.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">30 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Octavian takes Alexandria and Mark Antony takes his own life</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Octavian's army entered Alexandria and Mark Antony, defeated and deserted, killed himself. Cleopatra's suicide days later ended the Ptolemaic dynasty and Egypt became a Roman province.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1291</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swiss cantons swear the alliance celebrated as Switzerland's birth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Uri, Schwyz and Unterwalden concluded a perpetual defensive alliance, recorded in the Federal Charter dated early August 1291. 1 August is now Swiss National Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1714</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Anne dies, ending the Stuart line</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Queen Anne died without surviving children, the last Stuart monarch. Under the Act of Settlement the crown passed to George, Elector of Hanover, beginning the Hanoverian dynasty.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1774</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph Priestley isolates oxygen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By heating mercuric oxide, Joseph Priestley produced a gas in which a candle burned with remarkable vigour. He called it 'dephlogisticated air'; Lavoisier later named it oxygen.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1793</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France's Convention adopts the metric system</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The National Convention decreed a provisional metre, based on a fraction of the Earth's meridian, as France's unit of length. The decimal metric system has since been adopted almost worldwide.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1914</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany declares war on Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Russia refused to halt mobilisation, Germany declared war on it. The declaration turned the Austro-Serbian conflict into a general European war within days.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1944</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Warsaw Uprising begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Polish Home Army rose against the German occupiers of Warsaw. After 63 days, with the Red Army halted across the Vistula, the uprising was crushed and the city systematically destroyed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></li></ol>
